title: 'Decided: the buffer''s client holds the choice and names it in every save; the server keeps a copy for the redraws it starts.'
pid: 0af7f799-294e-4629-94b9-d6ac5da70b14
body: |2-
  A connection's views die with it, and a buffer outlives a server
  restart, so a choice kept only on the server would be lost while the
  buffer still showed it, and the next save's tamper check would then
  judge the user's carriers against the root author's chain and refuse.
  The client's buffer is the only thing that lives as long as the text
  it describes, so it is the authority, and a save says
  (overrides-followed . "user"); the server stores it in the view's
  state so that a redraw it was not asked for (another writer's change,
  a collateral redraw, a switch of the skgrepo restriction) follows it
  too. It survives saves, those redraws, and reconnects. The precedent
  is how a buffer of the diff view names its kind in each save.
